Completed initial investigation and proof of concept for the requested Container Info tab in Deployments-Dev → Wholeshestack-Bravo.

Work Completed
Added a custom TeamCity build step to generate a Container Info artifact (container-info.html) similar to the existing APAS-API Container Info tab.
Successfully configured TeamCity to publish the artifact and expose it through the Container Info tab.
Validated that the artifact is generated during deployment builds.
Tested multiple deployment runs in Bravo to verify artifact generation and visibility.
Current Findings

The Container Info tab is now being generated; however, it does not currently provide the information requested in the ticket.

The original request is specifically asking for:

Visibility into the actual deployed container image IDs/tags used by a deployment.
Ability to easily identify the Git commit SHA associated with a deployment.
Potential support for using a plain Git commit SHA as a Docker image tag.

Current output only displays image references and deployment configuration variables. It does not resolve the actual deployed image tags or container IDs in a way that satisfies the traceability requirements described in the ticket.

Blocker

There is currently uncertainty regarding the intended implementation and expected output.

The existing APAS-API Container Info tab appears to leverage TeamCity/Docker Registry metadata generated during image build and push operations, while the Wholeshestack deployment process only has access to deployment-time variables and stack configuration.

Additional guidance is needed from the ticket requester (Alex) and/or Ryan regarding:

Whether the goal is simply to expose deployed image tags in the deployment view.
Whether the goal is to expose full Git commit SHAs as deployment tags.
Whether changes are required in the image build pipeline rather than the deployment pipeline.
What specific output is expected in the Container Info tab.
